The MIT licence above covers the code in this repository (scripts/, viz/*.py,
viz/atlas.template.html). It does not cover the data or the third-party files
below, which keep their own licences.

1. Ofcom data (Open Government Licence v3.0)
   data/derived/exeter_readings.parquet, data/derived/exeter_grid_100m.gpkg,
   data/derived/exeter_grid_100m.json, the "cells" part of
   data/derived/exeter_map.json, and the figures shown in docs/index.html.

   Contains public sector information licensed under the Open Government
   Licence v3.0: https://www.nationalarchives.gov.uk/doc/open-government-licence/version/3/
   Sources: Ofcom, Mobile signal strength measurement data; Ofcom, Connected
   Nations 2025. The data has been filtered to an Exeter bounding box,
   cleaned, re-projected and aggregated to a 100 m grid. This project is not
   produced, approved or endorsed by Ofcom.

2. OpenStreetMap data (Open Database Licence v1.0)
   The "basemap" part of data/derived/exeter_map.json, also embedded in
   docs/index.html, is a derivative database of OpenStreetMap data and is
   made available under the Open Database Licence:
   https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1-0/
   (c) OpenStreetMap contributors, https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright

3. MapLibre GL JS (BSD-3-Clause)
   viz/maplibre-gl-4.7.1.css, also embedded in docs/index.html, is part of
   MapLibre GL JS. Its licence is reproduced in viz/MAPLIBRE-LICENSE.txt.
